  "grafo_evidencia": {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "94c8d524-7961-519a-b696-8614f7fe455f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Codex Escalada, Codex 1548\n- People: Juan Diego Cuauhtlatoatzin\n- Concepts: Our Lady of Guadalupe, Marian apparition\n- Places: Tepeyac, Mexico City, Mexico\n- Topics: Roman Catholic sainthood\n\nFacts:\n- Juan Diego Cuauhtlatoatzin, also known as Juan Diegotzil, lived from 1474 to 1548 and was a native of Mexico.\n- A Marian apparition of Our Lady of Guadalupe is said to have appeared to Juan Diego on four separate occasions in December 1531 on the hill of Tepeyac north of central Mexico City.\n- Codex Escalada, also called Codex 1548, is a sheet of parchment with ink drawings in the European style and supporting Nahuatl text depicting the apparition of Our Lady of Guadalupe to Juan Diego.\n- Juan Diego Cuauhtlatoatzin is recognized as the first Roman Catholic indigenous saint from the Americas.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a74f25ce-7f54-5af2-bf10-a4540ac23423",
        "text": "Page: Codex Escalada. Sentence: Codex Escalada (or Codex 1548) is a sheet of parchment on which there have been drawn, in ink and in the European style, images (with supporting Nahuatl text) depicting a Marian apparition, namely that of Our Lady of Guadalupe to Juan Diego which is said to have occurred on four separate occasions in December 1531 on the hill of Tepeyac north of central Mexico City.\nPage: Juan Diego. Sentence: Saint Juan Diego Cuauhtlatoatzin, also known as Juan Diegotzil (1474–1548), a native of Mexico, is the first Roman Catholic indigenous saint from the Americas.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
